{
  "sn8.7:0.1": "Linked Discourses 8.7 ",
  "sn8.7:0.2": "1. With Vaṅgīsa ",
  "sn8.7:0.3": "The Invitation to Admonish ",
  "sn8.7:1.1": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Sāvatthī in the stilt longhouse of Migāra’s mother in the Eastern Monastery, together with a large Saṅgha of around five hundred monks, all of whom were perfected ones. ",
  "sn8.7:1.2": "Now, at that time it was the sabbath—the full moon on the fifteenth day—and the Buddha was sitting in the open surrounded by the Saṅgha of monks for the invitation to admonish. ",
  "sn8.7:1.3": "Then the Buddha looked around the Saṅgha of monks, who were silent. He addressed them: ",
  "sn8.7:1.4": "“Come now, monks, I invite you all: ",
  "sn8.7:1.5": "Is there anything I’ve done by way of body or speech that you would criticize?” ",
  "sn8.7:2.1": "When he had spoken, Venerable Sāriputta rose from his seat, arranged his robe over one shoulder, raised his cupped palms toward the Buddha, and said: ",
  "sn8.7:2.2": "“There is nothing, sir, that you’ve done by way of body or speech that we would criticize. ",
  "sn8.7:2.3": "For the Blessed One gave rise to the unarisen path, gave birth to the unborn path, and explained the unexplained path. He is the knower of the path, the discoverer of the path, the expert on the path. ",
  "sn8.7:2.4": "And now the disciples live following the path; they acquire it later. ",
  "sn8.7:2.5": "And sir, I invite the Blessed One. ",
  "sn8.7:2.6": "Is there anything I’ve done by way of b